body:
Release-ready replacement for draft staging PR #20, using the exact same unchanged head `eef45ad43dec4193a4f01744339c89b8dfd9881a`.

Includes:
- preserved per-agent conversation round fold state across 800 ms live polling and redraws;
- unchanged-payload inspector stability;
- topology-aware multi-agent layout with lifecycle return edges excluded from rank;
- stable agent ordering, shared-tool/model bundling and separated ports;
- selection focus/fade behavior and incremental position stability;
- deterministic sanitized 7-agent Chromium regression fixture shared by live/static renderer validation.

Validated before reopening by Ruff, full pytest on Ubuntu/macOS/Windows, Chromium Viewer Agent Isolation, Provider Capability Stage Integrity, and Windows Launcher Compatibility. This PR is non-draft so it can follow the repository's normal squash-merge release flow.
